The plugins folder contains all core functionality for extending the game client's capabilities through modular components. It manages plugin lifecycle, execution, and communication while providing normalized data handling and dynamic CSS styling for each plugin. The registry.ts file serves as the central hub that accesses and coordinates all registered plugins within the game client application.

Per-line hot paths: plugin handlers run on EVERY received line, so anything built from config text is memoized on the last text (shared/memoLast.ts) and regex lists compile once per pattern (shared/regexCache.ts, bounded, cleared when full). Both return SHARED objects: treat parser results as read-only. pluginHost's getConfig() likewise returns one shared snapshot that setConfig/updateConfig drop, so a plugin must change settings through updateConfig, never by editing the returned object (it would leak into every later read). Mirrors the mobile app's memo-last.ts / plugin-host config memo; the mobile copy FREEZES the result, the web one does not so a missed in-place write degrades quietly instead of throwing inside an event handler.
